leadTermValuation -- The valuation defined by leading terms
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        v = leadTermValuation R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, the ring
        whose term order is used to define the valuation
  * Outputs:
      * v, an instance of the type *note Valuation: Valuation,, the lead term
        valuation

Description
===========

This function constructs a valuation which returns the negative exponent vector
of the lead term of a polynomial with respect to the ring's term order. The
valuation returns vectors in an ordered $\QQ$-module, which respects the
monomial order of the *note PolynomialRing: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,. For
more details see *note Ordered modules: Ordered modules,.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c, MonomialOrder => Lex];|
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : v = leadTermValuation R;            |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = 13*a^2*b + a*c^3;               |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i4 : g = 5*a^2*c + b^3;                  |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i5 : v f                                 |
|                                         |
|o5 = | -2 |                              |
|     | -1 |                              |
|     |  0 |                              |
|                                         |
|o5 : Ordered QQ^3 module                 |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i6 : v g                                 |
|                                         |
|o6 = | -2 |                              |
|     |  0 |                              |
|     | -1 |                              |
|                                         |
|o6 : Ordered QQ^3 module                 |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i7 : v f < v g                           |
|                                         |
|o7 = true                                |
+-----------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note valuation: valuation, -- User-defined valuation object
  * *note Valuation: Valuation, -- The type of all valuations
  * *note localRingValuation: localRingValuation, -- The valuation defined by a
    local ring.
  * *note lowestTermValuation: lowestTermValuation, -- The valuation defined by
    lowest terms
  * *note padicValuation: padicValuation, -- The p-adic valuation
  * *note trivialValuation: trivialValuation, -- The trivial valuation

Ways to use leadTermValuation:
==============================

  * "leadTermValuation(PolynomialRing)"

