orderedQQn -- Construct an ordered module $\QQ^n$
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = orderedQQn R
        M = orderedQQn(n, monomialOrders)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, polynomial
        ring for the construction
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, rank of the module
      * monomialOrder, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, monomial order for
        comparison
  * Outputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note OrderedQQn: OrderedQQn,, 

Description
===========

For an overview see *note Ordered modules: Ordered modules,. Let $R$ be a *note
polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing, with $n$ variables $x_1 \dots
x_n$. Then the corresponding ordered $\QQ^n$ module has the following ordering.
Suppose that $v, w \in \QQ^n$. Let $d \in \ZZ$ be a positive integer and $c \in
\ZZ^n_{\ge 0}$ be a vector such that $dv + c$ and $dw + c$ have non-negative
entries. Then $v < w$ if and only if $x^{dv + c} > x^{dw + c}$ in $R$. Note
that this property does not depend on the choices of $c$ and $d$, so we obtain
a well-defined order on $\QQ^n$.



+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_1 .. x_3, MonomialOrder => Lex]|
|                                             |
|o1 = R                                       |
|                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                          |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = orderedQQn R                        |
|                                             |
|       3                                     |
|o2 = QQ                                      |
|                                             |
|o2 : Ordered QQ^3 module                     |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : v = 1/2 * M_0 - 1/3 * M_1               |
|                                             |
|o3 = |  1/2 |                                |
|     | -1/3 |                                |
|     |   0  |                                |
|                                             |
|o3 : Ordered QQ^3 module                     |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : w = 1/2 * M_0 + 1/4 * M_2               |
|                                             |
|o4 = | 1/2 |                                 |
|     |  0  |                                 |
|     | 1/4 |                                 |
|                                             |
|o4 : Ordered QQ^3 module                     |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : v < w                                   |
|                                             |
|o5 = true                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+

Instead of supplying a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, we
may supply the rank $n$ of the module along with a monomial order. The
constructor creates the ring $R$ with $n$ variables and the given monomial
order to construct the *note OrderedQQn: OrderedQQn, module



+-----------------------------+
|i6 : N = orderedQQn(3, {Lex})|
|                             |
|       3                     |
|o6 = QQ                      |
|                             |
|o6 : Ordered QQ^3 module     |
+-----------------------------+
|i7 : R = N.cache.Ring        |
|                             |
|o7 = R                       |
|                             |
|o7 : PolynomialRing          |
+-----------------------------+
|i8 : N' = orderedQQn R       |
|                             |
|       3                     |
|o8 = QQ                      |
|                             |
|o8 : Ordered QQ^3 module     |
+-----------------------------+
|i9 : N == N'                 |
|                             |
|o9 = true                    |
+-----------------------------+

$N$ and $N'$ are the same module because they are built from the same ring. See
*note OrderedQQn == OrderedQQn: Ordered modules,.



See also
========

  * *note Ordered modules: Ordered modules, -- Overview of the ordered module
    $\QQ^n$
  * *note OrderedQQn: OrderedQQn, -- The class of all ordered modules $\QQ^n$

