Valuation -- The type of all valuations
***************************************

Description
===========

Valuation is a type that contains the data needed to evaluate a valuation. A
valuation is a function $v:R\rightarrow G\cup\{\infty\}$ where $R$ is a ring
and $G$ is a linearly ordered group with the following properties:

  * $v(ab)=v(a)+v(b)$,
  * $v(a+b)\geq\min\{v(a),v(b)\}$, and
  * $v(a)=\infty$ iff $a=0$.

This package provides common valuations and user-defined valuations.

See also
========

  * *note valuation: valuation, -- User-defined valuation object
  * *note leadTermValuation: leadTermValuation, -- The valuation defined by
    leading terms
  * *note lowestTermValuation: lowestTermValuation, -- The valuation defined by
    lowest terms
  * *note localRingValuation: localRingValuation, -- The valuation defined by a
    local ring.
  * *note padicValuation: padicValuation, -- The p-adic valuation
  * *note trivialValuation: trivialValuation, -- The trivial valuation

