valuation -- User-defined valuation object
******************************************

  * Usage: 
        v = valuation(f)
        v = valuation(f, S, T)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, the valuation function.
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a *note local ring:
        (LocalRings)LocalRing,, or an instance of the type *note Subring:
        (SubalgebraBases)Subring,, the source
      * T, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a *note local ring:
        (LocalRings)LocalRing,, or an instance of the type *note Subring:
        (SubalgebraBases)Subring,, the target
  * Outputs:
      * v, an instance of the type *note Valuation: Valuation,, user-defined
        valuation function

Description
===========

Construct a user defined valuation function. User-defined functions are not
checked for satisfying the properties of a valuation. It is not necessary to
specify a source or target, but if they are provided, then the input is checked
to be in the source (or either promotable to the source or in the fraction
field of the source). For common use cases, it is suggested to use the provided
valuations.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : v = valuation(x -> if x == 0 then infinity else 0)        |
|                                                               |
|o1 = valuation with unspecified source and target              |
|                                                               |
|o1 : Valuation                                                 |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : v = valuation(x -> if x == 0 then infinity else 0, ZZ, ZZ)|
|                                                               |
|o2 = valuation from ZZ to ZZ                                   |
|                                                               |
|o2 : Valuation                                                 |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

